sequenceDiagram
  %% Development uses the Gateway precheck in container/deploy-default.mmd. Production uses one shared native schedule; an Instance flag never changes its trigger or persisted pause.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: instance:auto-deploy:enable · Automatic deploys
  %% kind: instance.auto_deploy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  participant CLI as Caller<br/>CLI · MCP · API
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>policy · execution
  CLI->>GW: Enable auto-deploy<br/>instance:auto-deploy:enable
  Note over GW: Check placement<br/>record the flag
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - an active production Instance or a ready development container default; checkout working trees refuse
  %%> - a configured Project merge_check must be readable through the GitHub App
  %%> Result:
  %%> - sets the Instance's auto_deploy flag and resume point; starts no deployment
  %%> - warns with the Project name when no merge check is configured: every moved head deploys until one is set
  GW-->>CLI: Enabled Instance
  loop every minute, second 30
    Note over SW: Shared production schedule<br/>automatic-production-deploy
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the single native schedule discovers enabled production Instances from the Gateway
    %%> - keeps its persisted pause; enabling or disabling one Instance does not change this schedule
    SW->>GW: Read policy evidence<br/>Instance · history · checks
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the current deployed commit, target holder, resume point and Project merge_check
    %%> - finds the newest eligible green commit on the first-parent chain; a red or pending head can have an older green ancestor
    %%> - without a merge check, permits each moved head
    alt an eligible commit is due
      SW->>GW: Admit the pinned commit<br/>instance:deploy:automatic
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - saves a keyed intent before admission; the normal Gateway Instance lock excludes manual and automatic work
      GW->>SW: Run the deployment<br/>instance-deploy-direct
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - follows instance:deploy with the pinned commit and full admitted intent
      SW-->>GW: Deployment ended<br/>native terminal history
      %%> Result:
      %%> - records deployment history; failed attempts use the production retry and blocked-commit rules
    end
    SW->>GW: Publish the observation
    SW-->>GW: Policy fire ended<br/>captured event receipt
    %%> Result:
    %%> - records changed Activity and release alerts through the shared terminal reader
  end
  CLI->>GW: Disable auto-deploy<br/>instance:auto-deploy:disable
  Note over GW: Record the flag off
  %%> Result:
  %%> - skips this Instance on later scans and refuses automatic admission and queued execution
  %%> - a running deployment continues; manual deployment remains available
  GW-->>CLI: Disabled Instance
